  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 342 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nInto Thursday night and the day on Friday, mainly dry conditions \ncontinue as ridging moves across the area. However, an upper level \ndisturbance looks to move across the region out of northern Mexico \nand increase rain chances beginning late Friday and into Saturday \nmorning. The best rain chances will first exist out west before \nspreading to the east during Saturday. This system will be quick \nmoving and rain chances will quickly move to the east by Sunday. \nRain amounts will be on the lighter side with most locations \nreceiving just a few hundredths. A second low will move across the \nPanhandle and send a front through the region that will knock \ndaytime temperatures into the 50s for many early next week. The \npassage of this front will be dry. \n\n-Stickney",
